     "body": "<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=557058%3Ab97337af-3737-473c-9779-44d498499536\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"557058:b97337af-3737-473c-9779-44d498499536\" data-account-id=\"557058:b97337af-3737-473c-9779-44d498499536\" accountid=\"557058:b97337af-3737-473c-9779-44d498499536\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Harshakumar Ummerpillai</a>, You probably need to use a more recent build of the import utility to import without binaries.  You can download a current master build from: <a href=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/f4-artifacts/fcrepo-import-export-0.1.1-SNAPSHOT-0e42348f.jar\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://s3.amazonaws.com/f4-artifacts/fcrepo-import-export-0.1.1-SNAPSHOT-0e42348f.jar</a></p>\n\n<p>If you want to increase the logging, you can add the parameter \"-Dlog.fcrepo.importexport=DEBUG\".</p>",
